  "origin": "S2ORC (Semantic Scholar Open Research Corpus) is a large corpus of academic papers with full text extracted from PDFs, maintained by the Allen Institute for AI. S2ORC aggregates papers from many publishers (arXiv, PubMed Central, publisher portals); the underlying papers carry heterogeneous licenses (arXiv papers are often CC-BY or arXiv non-exclusive license; PubMed Central papers are under various PMC licenses including CC-BY, CC0, and publisher-specific terms; many publisher papers are under subscription-access terms that S2ORC redistributes under its own access agreement). The license field uses the agreement-supplied IRI per the interim convention in spec/0.0.1/index.md: S2ORC is obtained under AI2's terms (the Semantic Scholar data agreement) rather than under a single public license. This is the same pattern as Mímir's dbc dataset (agreement-supplied rather than public-license), but at much larger scale and with a more heterogeneous underlying-license mix — the per-document multi-license aggregate problem (Gap B) applies here too, layered on top of the agreement-supplied access. See notes/stress-test-bloom-roots.md. ROOTS was released as a gated subset subject to the BigScience ethical charter.",
